# AGENT CONTROL RULES

IMPORTANT

Never scan the entire repository unnecessarily.

When making changes:

- Read only files related to the task.
- Avoid recursive project-wide analysis.
- Avoid rebuilding architecture unless explicitly requested.
- Avoid touching unrelated files.
- Prefer surgical edits.

Before modifying more than five files:

Explain why.

Before creating new folders:

Explain why.

Before introducing a new dependency:

Explain why existing tools are insufficient.

---

# ANTI-AI-SLOP RULES

Never generate code merely to generate code.

Never create:

- unnecessary wrappers
- unnecessary abstractions
- unnecessary interfaces
- unnecessary helper classes
- unnecessary state providers
- unnecessary services

Every file must justify its existence.

Fewer files are preferred when functionality remains clear.

Prefer:

Readable > Clever

Simple > Complex

Working > Theoretical

Maintainable > Impressive

